"""Grading, without a model and without an instance (T2.5).

Two captures in, outcomes out — that is the whole contract, and it is why these tests cost
nothing. What is checked here is not "does the grader run" but that each kind can **fail**: a
check that cannot go red is coverage on paper, which is the failure mode this suite keeps
finding in itself (B2-B4, and the `n_skills` key that would have passed on every contaminated
run).

The two standing checks get the same treatment. `guards` had been validated as data since T2.2
and read by nobody; an emptied `guards:` was invisible. It is a graded outcome now.
"""

